{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I will give thanks</b> / <b>fearsome things</b> — a description of the acts, like: וידבר אתם קשות (and he spoke harshly with them)." "And the meaning of ונפשי יודעת מאד — according to R. Judah Halevi's view: 'His resting place is His glory's repose'; 'Your works are wondrous beyond me' even though my soul knows exceedingly. In my opinion: for it is connected, and thus it is: ונפשי יודעת מאד, and it testifies that wondrous are Your works. And R. Moses [ibn Ezra] said: for מאד is joined to נפלאים מעשיך, like: אל תעזבני עד מאד (do not forsake me exceedingly); this too is sound."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:13.142339258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}